<title>VENEZUELA: Venezuela M-0 drops 9.23 percent in week to Jan 10.</title>
<headline>Venezuela M-0 drops 9.23 percent in week to Jan 10.</headline>
<dateline>CARACAS 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Venezuela's monetary base fell 9.23 percent, or 151 billion bolivars, to 1.481 trillion bolivars in the week to January 10, the central bank said.</p>
<p>At the beginning of 1997, the money base was 1.66 trillion bolivars. At the beginning of 1996, it stood at 873 billion.</p>
<p>((-- Caracas newsroom, 582 505 2600))</p>
